  "source_shape_findings": [
    "Complete C-shaped main with north/east four occupied storeys, south three-storey low roof, partial B1 and three shared stair cores. Real court/gallery air and backing walls retained. No fictitious extra full storey, no court infill.",
    "Connected two-storey annex retains two projecting stairs,1F side and lower-room projections and local mezzanine. Two negative closed hall-void boundaries are optional approximate interiors, not evidence of whole-floor lightwells. Selected neck length is not paper-break whitespace measured as distance.",
    "798 outer-east candidate retains true recessed entrance, visible door/landing/steps, single-floor lattice with upper glass/white-beam band and forward round piers. Unknown rear facade stays restrained, not mirrored. Grade/support proxies are limited to building/arrival contact, not full landscape.",
    "799 southwest view of the southern low wing gives the better bounded near-left/receding-right handedness and three visible window rows. Medium confidence, not unique surveyed camera or geodetic compass. Rejected northern-facade window/stair trial withdrawn.",
    "Single limited northern roof enclosure is a coarse photo-supported volume approximation, not a claim that798/799 show one actual enclosure. Exact roof count/location/use/size lack independent roof survey. Distant long-lens798 test establishes visibility feasibility only; earlier smaller-box occlusion tests retained as history. No new tower or whole floor added to force a match.",
    "Raw Boolean original-run material provenance retained; no nearest-face paint. Annex white diagonal artifact and main front opaque/grille conflicts corrected in generator.799 terminal rail/post micro-lip independently localized at old0.013842mm and fixed by a true construction overlap before finalfreeze; no raw-face deletion or QA relaxation.",
    "Nine final authored PNGs are mesh renders/coordinate diagram only, no source pixels. All original source photos/plan overlays stay external private evidence."
  ],
